 - [ ] **REG-002**: When a lookup completes, the system SHALL include the active snapshot date in the result.
 - [ ] **REG-003**: When a snapshot has an invalid signature, an unsupported schema version, or duplicate serial numbers, the system SHALL reject the import and retain the active snapshot.
 - [ ] **REG-004**: When a valid replacement snapshot is activated, the system SHALL expose all of its records together without exposing a partially imported snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-005**: When a valid snapshot is imported, the system SHALL build a new SQLite index in a temporary file and atomically replace the active index file only after the build completes successfully.
+- [ ] **REG-006**: When the active index file is missing or corrupt on startup, the system SHALL treat it as no active snapshot and require a valid USB import before lookups succeed.
+- [ ] **REG-007**: When a lookup encounters an I/O error reading the index, the system SHALL return a registry-unavailable error distinct from NotFound.
+- [ ] **REG-008**: When a snapshot import encounters an I/O error, the system SHALL roll back to the previous index and report the failure reason.
+- [ ] **REG-009**: When a serial-number lookup executes, the system SHALL complete within 250 ms p99 on the target kiosk hardware.
+- [ ] **REG-010**: When a 150 MB snapshot with 90,000 records is imported, the system SHALL complete the import within 5 seconds.
